{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A sorted set kept in a treap: a binary search tree whose vertices also carry random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"priorities, with no vertex of higher priority than its parent (Seidel and Aragon, 1996).","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The random priorities make the shape that of a random binary search tree, whatever order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements arrive in, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time. A treap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also splits at an element into the elements below it and the rest, and joins two treaps whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements don’t interleave. The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed by rank like an array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treap[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The priorities come from a random number generator given at creation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator"},{"text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The treap draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"priorities as its original.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the treap holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree"],"title":"Sorted sets","generated":true,"anchor":"Sorted-sets"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"Treap","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:17BinarySearchTrees5TreapV","modules":[{"name":"BinarySearchTrees"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap.swift#L31","fileName":"Treap.swift"}},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/Split"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(_:using:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(using:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/height"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\